        // The Wake's wave: the plasma gathered across the projector's mouth is let go as one
        // wall that rolls out over 400 m of ground. Not a gun: the pinch dumping its pressure
        // (a soft-edged whoomp with a rough growl in it, no crack), then the wave surging away
        // as a roaring, searing rush that holds for most of a second, spreads across the
        // stereo field as the front widens, and recedes as it runs out, its plasma crackling
        // as it breaks and cools. The weight sits in the low mids, not the sub, so it carries
        // on small speakers; done well before the next shot 2.6 s later. No tone falls above
        // the low mids, no pitched layer rings out.
